{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Ethernet switch feels like a plausible next step after my USB Ethernet adapter and patch cables because it could help connect more wired devices, although I may not need sixteen ports.",
    "The microSD card connects directly to my previous removable-storage purchases and Raspberry Pi setup, provided my intended device supports its capacity."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The RAM, internal SSD, fan and CPU cooler assume I am upgrading a desktop, while my history mainly shows accessories for connecting, organizing and maintaining devices.",
    "The SSD enclosure needs a spare compatible drive I have not indicated owning, and the router needs a replacement reason that my cable purchases do not establish.",
    "The drawing display has no clear connection to my activities, and having bought a Kindle does not mean I currently need a general-purpose tablet."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in computer accessories seems to have been stretched into an interest in any desktop component.",
    "Buying networking accessories seems to have been treated as a reason to replace major networking equipment, even though I may simply be connecting existing devices."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent adapter, cables, headphone mount and duster suggest practical improvements to an existing setup rather than a new computer build.",
    "Compatibility and a concrete use matter: I need a supported device for a larger microSD card, a spare drive for an enclosure, and enough wired devices to justify a large switch.",
    "My purchases occur in distinct bursts separated by long gaps, so an older Raspberry Pi or Kindle purchase does not establish an ongoing upgrade project."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in connectivity and removable storage, but stretched practical setup purchases into unsupported assumptions about desktop upgrades and new devices."
}"}
